1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,504
The bet connects a hypothesis to the smallest
action and evidence that would change your mind.

2
00:00:05,574 --> 00:00:07,110
State it before acting.

3
00:00:07,180 --> 00:00:11,788
A falsifiable bet names the uncertainty
rather than promising a win.

4
00:00:11,858 --> 00:00:15,549
Define stop conditions as
well as desired performance.

5
00:00:15,619 --> 00:00:21,336
Practical stop conditions may include
unsafe actions, unusable data, insufficient

6
00:00:21,406 --> 00:00:23,795
authorization, or user rejection.

7
00:00:23,865 --> 00:00:28,452
Record who can make the gate decision
and what happens when evidence is mixed.

8
00:00:28,522 --> 00:00:33,791
The hypothesis is that repeated category
lookup causes avoidable review effort.

9
00:00:33,861 --> 00:00:36,699
A routing suggestion tests that mechanism.

10
00:00:36,769 --> 00:00:42,230
An automatic-reply generator changes a
different part of the workflow and introduces

11
00:00:42,300 --> 00:00:43,623
additional risk.

12
00:00:43,693 --> 00:00:48,471
Pause the video and complete this exercise
before opening the worked response.

13
00:00:48,541 --> 00:00:53,661
Write a bet, a smallest action, and two pieces
of evidence that would change your decision.

14
00:00:53,731 --> 00:00:59,534
If category lookup dominates effort, a reviewable
suggestion should reduce defined review

15
00:00:59,604 --> 00:01:03,295
time. Test one ticket category
with twelve simulated tasks.

16
00:01:03,365 --> 00:01:09,082
Change direction if the suggestion creates
more checking work or breaches the agreed error

17
00:01:09,152 --> 00:01:12,864
limit. Stop immediately if it
sends a message without approval.

18
00:01:12,934 --> 00:01:16,859
A failed hypothesis can still be
a successful learning experiment.

19
00:01:16,929 --> 00:01:19,511
When should you define disconfirming evidence?

20
00:01:19,581 --> 00:01:21,607
A. Before the experiment B.

21
00:01:21,677 --> 00:01:23,405
After seeing the results C.

22
00:01:23,475 --> 00:01:25,225
Only if the sponsor asks.

23
00:01:25,295 --> 00:01:26,745
The best answer is A.

24
00:01:26,815 --> 00:01:29,610
Precommitment reduces moving the goalposts.
